<p>Needs a more clinical tone. The concept is interesting, though.</p>
<p>One more note: normally, I'd say that "give him what he wants" is not a containment procedure, but this one did it correctly: luxuries are rewards for cooperation, and this SCP seems very cooperative. In addition, the line about making sure not to get emotionally attached is good as well. I'd put limits on the luxuries he's allowed, though, just to make sure that people know we're talking reasonable luxuries like reading materials, not things like gold plated toilets.</p>

