<p>the thing about emotional attachments and the commands about luxury are actually interesting because they changed the way i view SCP reports. like in this report, its not the head of the security around the object writing this report and handing it out to his underlings, its some independent investigator writing his report and giving it to the head of security. i don't know if everyone interprets this way, but thats the way i see it now. if you notice, i don't really have any specific commands, any exact rules, like the cell has to be this wide or he gets this. its more like this guy needs this, schedule this, be warned of this, now you figure out the details. its a general plan, with these key words, like human class living quarters. I imagined the security guy having to flip through a handbook, look at human class living quarters, go ok he needs this and this, and then write down notes, apply signs, and give directions.</p>

